course: dictionary
lesson: 2715
title: Dimetrodon: not a dinosaur
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may never have met the word dimetrodon before, and that is fine. Read the words around it for clues. «Dimetrodon, with its sail, lived about 280 million years ago, before any dinosaurs» tells you it is an animal from very long ago, and that it had a sail.
explain: The sentence also tells you what dimetrodon is not. It is named as lived before any dinosaurs, so it is not one of them, even though toy sets often sell it next to the dinosaurs.
explain: Look at the list in the second sentence: «pterosaurs... were not dinosaurs; neither were plesiosaurs, ichthyosaurs or Dimetrodon.» The word neither tells you the same thing about all of them. Context can be a clue that corrects a wrong idea you had.
fact: Dimetrodon was a large animal with a tall sail on its back.
fact: It lived about 295 to 272 million years ago, before the dinosaurs.
fact: Dimetrodon was not a dinosaur. It was a synapsid.
fact: Synapsids are more closely related to mammals than to dinosaurs, so dimetrodon is more closely related to us than to dinosaurs.
fact: Its sail may have helped it warm up or show off.
exercise: What is dimetrodon? | *A large animal with a tall sail on its back | A dinosaur with wings | A plant that grows in the sea
exercise: According to the sentence, when did dimetrodon live? | About 2 million years ago, with early people | Only after the dinosaurs had died out | *About 280 million years ago, before any dinosaurs
exercise: Which animal in the sentence had a wingspan of about 10 metres? | Ichthyosaur | Plesiosaur | Dimetrodon | *Quetzalcoatlus
test: What does synapsid tell us about dimetrodon? | *It is more closely related to mammals than to dinosaurs | It lived in trees near the sea | It is a kind of dinosaur with wings
test: The sail may have helped dimetrodon do what? | *Warm up | Fly over the sea | Sing loudly to other animals
exam: Dimetrodon lived before the dinosaurs. What does that tell us about it? | *It was not a dinosaur | It was a dinosaur with a sail | It was a dinosaur that lived with people
